From 3419288401da088811938d9a01a1de72a656f986 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:48:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 500/503] [KV] VLLM_KV_CACHE_POISON: new blocks filled with NaN
 bytes, not zeros (debug)

vLLM zeroes newly allocated KV blocks when the cache mixes precisions
(needs_kv_cache_zeroing), since a block reused across groups would decode
another precision's stale bytes. Whether a model's kernels need that, or
only mask unwritten slots by select, is not visible from the outputs: a
kernel that reads an unwritten slot, or masks one arithmetically
(0 * x, x + -inf), sees zeros and stays finite.

The debug switch VLLM_KV_CACHE_POISON (off by default, never in serving)
fills each new block with all-ones bytes instead: NaN in FP32, BF16, FP16,
FP8 E4M3 and E5M2 and UE8M0 at every byte offset (E2M1 reads -6.0, beside a
NaN UE8M0 scale). Such a read then turns its output NaN. The switch forces
the fill for caches that skip zeroing and also fills the compressor ring's
CircularBufferSpec blocks, which zeroing never touches. Warmup compiles the
fill on the null block with zeros, which leaves it as zeroing does.

The fill is its own TileLang kernel, fill_kv_blocks_kernel: the zeroing
kernel's segments, pages and predicated stores with a word argument,
declared in its place under the switch, so the frozen kernel cache accepts
it. With the switch off nothing changes: the zeroing kernel, its key and its
declaration are as before, and no fill is declared or compiled.

On DeepSeek V4.1 Flash zeroing runs only because the compressor ring is
FP32 beside byte pages; it costs 0.20% of a 15K-token prefill and nothing
measurable in decode.

Tests (CPU): the zeroer fills where it zeroes, the warmup's zero null
block, the declared kernel by mode, the poison bytes as NaN in each float
format, the forced fill, DS4.1's ring as the only mixed precision, the ring
manager recording its block under the switch. GPU: the TileLang fill writes
the word exactly where the Triton zeroing clears, and launches only its
declared call.
